---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Leadership in the AI Era" description="Human-centered perspectives from Dr. Ramesh Kayyam on artificial intelligence, leadership, change, and the future of work.">
  <section class="leadership-hero">
    <div class="signal signal-one" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="signal signal-two" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="container hero-content"><p class="eyebrow">Leadership in the AI Era</p><h1>The future may be technological. Leadership must remain human.</h1><p>Artificial intelligence is reshaping how we work, decide, learn, and lead. The essential question is not simply what technology can do—but how we choose to use it.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/speaking">Invite Dr. Ramesh</a><a class="button button--ghost" href="#principles">Explore the principles</a></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="paper section north-star"><div class="container north-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">A human-centered north star</p><h2 class="section-title">Technology changes the tools in our hands. Leadership shapes the future we create.</h2></div><div><p>For Dr. Ramesh Kayyam, leadership is not about choosing humanity or innovation. It is about ensuring that innovation remains accountable to humanity.</p><p>The leaders who will make the greatest difference are those who combine strategic clarity with empathy, curiosity with responsibility, and technological intelligence with human wisdom.</p></div></div></section>

  <section id="principles" class="section principles-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">The principles</p><h2 class="section-title">Four ways to lead through change.</h2><div class="principles-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Lead with ethics</h3><p>Use AI and emerging technologies in ways that protect dignity, fairness, trust, and accountability.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Keep people at the center</h3><p>Design change around human needs, meaningful work, and the potential of people to grow.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Build adaptive cultures</h3><p>Help organizations learn, experiment, communicate, and respond with resilience in uncertain moments.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Choose purpose over noise</h3><p>Focus attention on the questions, decisions, and outcomes that genuinely create long-term value.</p></article></div></div></section>

  <section class="paper section questions"><div class="container questions-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Questions worth leading</p><h2 class="section-title">The questions we ask determine the future we build.</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div><p class="intro-text">Talkintree explores these questions through writing, research, teaching, workshops, and conversations.</p></div><div class="question-list"><p><span>01</span> How can leaders use AI without losing human judgment?</p><p><span>02</span> What does ethical innovation look like in practice?</p><p><span>03</span> How can organizations prepare people—not only systems—for change?</p><p><span>04</span> What kind of future is worth building together?</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="section practice"><div class="container practice-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">From ideas into action</p><h2 class="section-title">A conversation that can move from reflection to practice.</h2><p class="section-copy">These ideas are developed through three connected forms of work—each designed to make leadership more thoughtful, practical, and human.</p></div><div class="practice-cards"><article><b>01</b><h3>Writing & Thought Leadership</h3><p>Accessible reflections on AI, leadership, change, and human potential.</p><a href="/blog">Visit Thought Garden ↗</a></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Speaking & Workshops</h3><p>Engaging talks for organizations, universities, and leadership communities.</p><a href="/speaking">Explore speaking ↗</a></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Learning & Mentoring</h3><p>Educational experiences that encourage curiosity, growth, and courageous action.</p><a href="/contact">Start a conversation ↗</a></article></div></div></section>

  <section class="leadership-cta"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Bring the conversation to your community</p><h2>Let’s build a future worthy of the people who will live in it.</h2><a class="button" href="/contact">Connect with Dr. Ramesh</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .leadership-hero{position:relative;overflow:hidden;min-height:710px;padding:11rem 0 6rem;background:radial-gradient(circle at 78% 22%,#294833 0,#142119 38%,#0d0d0d 75%)}.leadership-hero:after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;background:repeating-radial-gradient(ellipse at 92% 85%,transparent 0 6.5%,rgba(214,181,107,.07) 6.6% 7.1%,transparent 7.2% 14%);mask-image:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent 25%,black)}.hero-content{position:relative;z-index:2;max-width:920px}.hero-content h1{font-size:clamp(3.55rem,7vw,6.75rem);letter-spacing:-.07em;margin:.85rem 0 1.25rem}.hero-content>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:665px;color:#d5cec1;font-size:1.12rem}.hero-actions{display:flex;gap:.8rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:2.2rem}.signal{position:absolute;z-index:1;border:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.24);border-radius:50%;animation:pulse 6s ease-in-out infinite}.signal-one{width:500px;height:500px;right:-120px;bottom:-240px}.signal-two{width:320px;height:320px;right:55px;bottom:-160px;animation-delay:1.8s}
  .north-grid,.questions-grid,.practice-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:7rem}.north-grid>div:last-child{font-size:1.08rem;color:#59544b}.north-grid>div:last-child p:first-child{margin-top:0}.principles-section{background:#111}.principles-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);margin-top:3.5rem;border-top:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.32);border-left:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.32)}.principles-grid article{min-height:290px;padding:1.55rem;border-right:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.32);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.32);transition:.25s ease}.principles-grid article:hover{background:#1d1d1b;transform:translateY(-5px)}.principles-grid span,.practice-cards b{color:var(--gold);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em}.principles-grid h3{font-size:1.65rem;margin:2.5rem 0 .6rem}.principles-grid p{color:#c6bfb4;font-size:.91rem;margin:0}.questions-grid{align-items:start}.intro-text{color:#5a544b;font-size:1.02rem;max-width:500px}.question-list{border-top:1px solid #d9d0c0}.question-list p{margin:0;padding:1.1rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d9d0c0;color:#49443c;font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.18rem;line-height:1.35}.question-list span{display:inline-block;width:2rem;color:#896b30;font-family:'DM Sans',Arial,sans-serif;font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;vertical-align:middle}.practice{background:linear-gradient(120deg,#152018,#111)}.practice-grid{align-items:start}.practice-grid .section-copy{margin-top:1.5rem}.practice-cards{border-top:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.32)}.practice-cards article{padding:1.25rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.32);display:grid;grid-template-columns:80px 1fr auto;gap:1rem;align-items:center}.practice-cards h3{font-size:1.25rem;margin:0}.practice-cards p{grid-column:2;color:#c1b9ad;font-size:.9rem;margin:0}.practice-cards a{grid-column:3;grid-row:1 / span 2;color:var(--gold-light);font-size:.66rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;white-space:nowrap}.leadership-cta{text-align:center;padding:6.3rem 1rem;background:var(--gold);color:var(--ink)}.leadership-cta h2{font-size:clamp(2.55rem,5.5vw,4.6rem);max-width:880px;margin:.7rem auto 1.75rem}.leadership-cta .eyebrow{color:#5b461b}.leadership-cta .button{background:#111;color:var(--ivory);border-color:#111}@keyframes pulse{50%{transform:scale(1.08);opacity:.5}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.signal{animation:none}}@media(max-width:950px){.principles-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.north-grid,.questions-grid,.practice-grid{gap:4rem}}@media(max-width:720px){.leadership-hero{padding-top:9rem;min-height:640px}.north-grid,.questions-grid,.practice-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2.5rem}.practice-cards article{grid-template-columns:1fr}.practice-cards p,.practice-cards a{grid-column:auto;grid-row:auto}.practice-cards a{margin-top:.4rem}}@media(max-width:520px){.principles-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hero-content h1{font-size:3.4rem}}
</style>
